            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0000000000000539</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Extraluminal air can occur through a wide variety of mechanisms. Often, the free air resides in isolated regions including the thorax, the peritoneum, or the mediastinum. We present a pediatric case where there was extensive extraluminal air simultaneously within several regions, one of which has never been reported in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
